  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🛸 Futuristic Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Sleek first names and global surnames for science fiction characters."
    },
    "intro": "Future names in good science fiction aren't random letters: they're today's names, worn smooth and mixed by a few centuries of travel. This **futuristic name generator** pairs short, sleek first names with surnames from all over the world, and double-barrelled ones for when families merge.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What future names really sound like",
        "content": "<p>In good science fiction, future names aren't random letters: they're today's names, worn smooth and mixed by centuries of travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Mixing:</strong> when people move, names travel with them, so a future crew list mixes surnames from every continent.</li><li><strong>Double-barrelled</strong> surnames join two families, as many families already do: Elara Okafor-Lindqvist.</li><li><strong>Sleek first names</strong> like Kael, Nova and Elowen are short, easy to say over a radio and hard to place in any one century.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming your crew",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Choose First name</strong> for a single name, <strong>Full name</strong> for a first name and surname, or <strong>Double-barrelled</strong> for a joined surname.</li><li><strong>Mix it up:</strong> a crew where every name comes from one place will feel like today, not the future.</li><li><strong>Famous names</strong> like Shepard, Ripley, Deckard and Atreides are left out.</li></ul><p>For the ship they fly, try the <a href=\"spaceship-name-generator.html\">Spaceship Name Generator</a>, for the planet they're headed to, the <a href=\"planet-name-generator.html\">Planet Name Generator</a>, and for the city they left, the <a href=\"cyberpunk-name-generator.html\">Cyberpunk Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For the rest of the future, see all the <a href=\"../categories/scifi-names.html\">sci-fi name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What's a good futuristic name?",
        "answer": "A short, sleek first name like Kael or Elara with a surname from anywhere in the world, or a double-barrelled one, like Elara Okafor-Lindqvist."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do you make a name sound futuristic?",
        "answer": "Mix names from different cultures, keep first names short, and join surnames. Random letters tend to sound silly rather than futuristic."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's a good name for a spaceship captain?",
        "answer": "A full name with a strong surname, like Tarek Vasquez-Oduya. Choose Full name or Double-barrelled."
      }
    ]
  }
